ID  - SG-B87C98DE3C1D
TI  - Anaerobic production of alginate by Pseudomonas aeruginosa: alginate restricts diffusion of oxygen
AU  - D J Hassett
JO  - Journal of Bacteriology
PY  - 1996
DO  - 10.1128/jb.178.24.7322-7325.1996
AB  - <jats:p>Pseudomonas aeruginosa produced alginate and elevated algD (encoding GDPmannose 6-dehydrogenase) transcription under strict anaerobic conditions, especially when using nitrate as a terminal electron acceptor. Purified alginate added to bacterial suspensions caused a decrease in growth, suggesting that alginate contributes to oxygen limitation for the organism and likely for patients afflicted with the inherited autosomal disease cystic fibrosis.</jats:p>
